{
  "comment": "Capture spec for docs/images; docs/_capture/README.md describes the procedure. DocsCapture.cs writes <raw>/<en|ru|shared>/<id>.png+.json; annotate.py crops and numbers them. folder 'lang' = one image per language in docs/images/en|ru, 'shared' = docs/images/shared. width = displayed width in the Markdown <img width>. Crop edges: 'content', 'full', or left/top/right/bottom as a number in points or {anchor, edge, pad}; pad is in points. Anchors match the layout JSON: type, class, name, binding, text (string or {en,ru}), textStarts, textContains, index; or px [x,y,w,h] / [x,y] in points (annotate.py multiplies them by the layout's ppp, so they hold at any display scale). An anchor can be a list of alternatives; the first one that matches an element is used. hint = text added to the error when no element matches. place: left (default), right, top-right, top-left, above, above-left, below, below-left, center; force keeps left at the image edge; dx/dy in displayed pixels.",
